abstract: >-
  A calibration / fairness / uncertainty audit of five routine-data machine
  learning model families (logistic regression, random forest, XGBoost,
  LightGBM, MLP) predicting significant liver fibrosis (VCTE LUXSMED >= 8.2
  kPa) from ten routine demographic, anthropometric, and laboratory predictors
  in NHANES 2017-March 2020 (N=7,153). Finds comparable discrimination and
  adequate aggregate calibration across model families, but a large,
  reproduced BMI-sensitivity disparity and subgroup conformal under-coverage
  (BMI-Obese, Age 60+) that no tested mitigation resolves. See
  liver_fibrosis_research/REPOSITORY_MAP.md for the full repository structure
  and liver_fibrosis_research/documentation/final_research_audit/DO_NOT_CLAIM.md
  for claims this evidence base does not support.
